review_comments:
Hmm, on closer inspection both formats seem kind of strange to me, especially if the comment value contains line breaks. Could this possibly be
```json
{
    "property":
    /*comment*/
    "value"
}
```
But that's just me. Do we have any examples of other (non .NET) JSON formatters that handle comments?

@krwq @layomia opinions?

@eiriktsarpalis what you proposed makes sense to me but also:

```json
{
    "property": /*comment*/
    "value"
}
```

would look good to me, I'm not strongly opinionated here - it seems like a weird place to put comment to me anyway
